{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "f34db825-436a-41bb-b33b-b433e102cbcb"/*HandLandmarkDetectionExample*/,
  "Description": "Detects hands in a live camera image and shows the built-in debug view: the camera frame with all 21 landmarks of every detected hand.\n\nTurn [Debug] off to get the clean camera image on [OutputTexture] instead. The detected hands are provided as data: [PointBuffer] holds 21 points per hand in centered image coordinates (Y up, X and Y in roughly -1..1, Z scaled by [ZScale]), each point carrying its landmark index (0 = wrist, 9 = middle finger base) in F1 and a visibility estimate in F2. [WorldLandmarksBuffer] holds the same hands in metric world space, [HandCount] the number of hands.\n\nSee [MaxHands] and the three confidence thresholds for tuning, [Acceleration] for the inference delegate, and [ConstantSize] to lock the landmark cloud's size regardless of the hand's distance to the camera.",
  "InputUis": [],
